1
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:09,790
B1.

2
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:15,440
Nora is listening to a podcast about how to make potato stamps.

3
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:20,810
Listen to it and put the following instructions in the correct order.

4
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:24,810
Write the numbers 1 to 7 in the blanks.

5
00:00:24,810 --> 00:00:29,210
Today we're going to make potato stamps.

6
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:32,660
Potato stamps are very easy to make.

7
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:35,910
First, you should get a large potato.

8
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:40,580
Don't use a small one, it'll be too difficult to hold.

9
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:43,080
Next, wash it carefully.

10
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:46,420
You should be sure to get it really clean.

11
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:49,160
Now cut it in half with a knife.

12
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:53,840
Be careful, I don't want anyone to get hurt.

13
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:59,770
Next, you should draw a design on the flat side of the potato with a pen.

14
00:00:59,770 --> 00:01:03,950
Then carefully cut the design out with your knife.

15
00:01:03,950 --> 00:01:07,510
After that, put some paint on a plate.

16
00:01:07,510 --> 00:01:11,650
Put the flat side of your potato in the paint.

17
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:16,180
Finally, put the potato on a piece of paper.

18
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:18,020
Isn't that fun?

19
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:20,570
You have a potato stamp now.
